1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:07,870
Professor: Lá nos irregulares eu avisei que vinha um ajudante pro passado. Chegou. Pra dizer 'eu não fui', escuta como o inglês faz:

2
00:00:08,370 --> 00:00:09,438
Professor: I didn't go.

3
00:00:10,664 --> 00:00:11,779
Bia: I didn't go.

4
00:00:13,755 --> 00:00:16,634
Professor: E pra perguntar 'você viu isso?'? Escuta:

5
00:00:17,134 --> 00:00:18,202
Professor: Did you see it?

6
00:00:20,005 --> 00:00:21,259
Bia: Did you see it?

7
00:00:21,759 --> 00:00:29,607
Bia: Peraí — então o 'went' vira 'go' de novo? O passado pula pro 'did', e o verbo relaxa — igual o 'doesn't'!

8
00:00:30,693 --> 00:00:37,520
Professor: Cravou — você mesma ligou! O 'did' carrega o passado, o verbo fica pelado. 'você trabalhou ontem?':

9
00:00:41,027 --> 00:00:42,885
Bia: Did you work yesterday?

10
00:00:43,941 --> 00:00:45,938
Professor: 'eu trabalhei ontem, mas eu não estudei':

11
00:00:49,371 --> 00:00:52,575
Bia: I worked yesterday, but I didn't study.

12
00:00:53,679 --> 00:00:54,794
Professor: 'ela não trabalhou':

13
00:00:57,884 --> 00:00:59,231
Bia: She didn't work.

14
00:01:00,867 --> 00:01:03,003
Professor: 'ela tava cansada, então ela não trabalhou':

15
00:01:06,829 --> 00:01:09,244
Bia: She was tired, so she didn't work.

16
00:01:10,429 --> 00:01:11,544
Professor: 'eles não estudaram':

17
00:01:14,767 --> 00:01:16,207
Bia: They didn't study.

18
00:01:18,148 --> 00:01:20,006
Professor: 'eu estudei, mas eu não fui pra casa':

19
00:01:23,953 --> 00:01:26,368
Bia: I studied, but I didn't go home.

20
00:01:28,233 --> 00:01:29,208
Professor: 'você me viu?':

21
00:01:32,604 --> 00:01:33,811
Bia: Did you see me?

22
00:01:36,275 --> 00:01:39,712
Professor: E a resposta curta ecoa o 'did': 'você foi? — sim':

23
00:01:42,758 --> 00:01:43,965
Bia: Yes, I did.

24
00:01:46,252 --> 00:01:46,995
Professor: 'e não':

25
00:01:50,284 --> 00:01:51,491
Bia: No, I didn't.

26
00:01:52,707 --> 00:01:54,750
Professor: 'eu não fui' — rápido, de novo:

27
00:01:57,867 --> 00:01:59,260
Bia: I didn't went?

28
00:01:59,760 --> 00:02:05,240
Bia: ...não, peraí — o passado já tá no 'didn't', o verbo volta pelado. I didn't go.

29
00:02:07,464 --> 00:02:11,922
Professor: Isso — um passado SÓ, no 'did'; não bota duas vezes. De novo:

30
00:02:15,102 --> 00:02:16,217
Bia: I didn't go.

31
00:02:18,089 --> 00:02:23,662
Professor: Sente o par numa frase — afirmativo contra negativo: 'eu fui, mas ele não foi':

32
00:02:27,300 --> 00:02:29,065
Bia: I went, but he didn't go.

33
00:02:30,623 --> 00:02:32,759
Professor: 'eu fui pra casa, mas eu não vi isso':

34
00:02:36,306 --> 00:02:38,674
Bia: I went home, but I didn't see it.

35
00:02:39,768 --> 00:02:44,458
Professor: Agora com um irregular: 'você teve um carro?' — o 'had' volta pra 'have':

36
00:02:47,517 --> 00:02:49,003
Bia: Did you have a car?

37
00:02:50,311 --> 00:02:53,283
Professor: 'ela não disse isso' — o 'said' volta pra 'say':

38
00:02:56,963 --> 00:02:58,356
Bia: She didn't say it.

39
00:02:59,997 --> 00:03:01,622
Professor: 'ele tava lá, mas ele não me viu':

40
00:03:04,936 --> 00:03:07,676
Bia: He was there, but he didn't see me.

41
00:03:09,554 --> 00:03:10,808
Professor: 'você me ligou ontem?':

42
00:03:14,261 --> 00:03:15,979
Bia: Did you call me yesterday?

43
00:03:17,428 --> 00:03:23,187
Professor: E o be — ele entra nessa máquina do 'did' também? Pensa: 'você tava cansado?':

44
00:03:26,981 --> 00:03:28,374
Bia: Were you tired?

45
00:03:30,422 --> 00:03:40,174
Professor: Isso! O be NÃO chama o 'did' — ele pergunta sozinho, virando na frente, nunca 'Did you were'. O resto chama o 'did'. Fecha com a do dia a dia: 'você viu isso?':

46
00:03:43,418 --> 00:03:44,672
Bia: Did you see it?

47
00:03:46,533 --> 00:03:55,310
Professor: Sacou? No passado, chama o 'did' e o verbo fica PELADO — e o be pergunta sozinho. É a máquina do 'du', um passo pra trás no tempo.

48
00:03:57,097 --> 00:04:05,224
Bia: Boa — 'Did you see it?'. O 'did' carrega o passado, o verbo relaxa. Agora eu pergunto e nego sobre o que já foi!

